summary:
  The bitrate sort forgets the probe's verdict and lifts a dead 320 over the living.

history:
  The probe sinks a station that does not answer under the ones that do,
  and every later answer of a bitrate search sorts the whole list again.
  A sort that reads only the number would put the dead back on top each
  time a pass lands; this is that sort.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
          keyed.push({ at: i, dead: r.alive === 0 ? 1 : 0,

replace:
          keyed.push({ at: i, dead: 0,

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_searchlogic.qml::test_a_dead_row_stays_under_the_living_in_its_own_order.
  Line-neutral.
